from pathlib import Path
import json
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
P=Path(__file__).parent;R=P/'results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified'
def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())
df=pd.read_csv(R/'summary.csv');diag=read(R/'rank_diagnostics.json');fits=read(R/'factorizations.json')
# Flat per-epoch estimates/loadings supplement the complete frozen JSON.
est=[];loads=[]
for key,f in fits.items():
 run,kernel,k=key.rsplit('_',2)
 for i,e in enumerate(f['epochs']):
  est.append(dict(run=run,kernel=kernel,k=int(k),epoch=e,estimate=f['rank1']['scores'][i],triplet_initial=f['rank1']['initial'][i],triplets=f['rank1']['triplet_counts'][i]))
  loads.append(dict(run=run,kernel=kernel,k=int(k),epoch=e,component1=f['rank2']['loadings'][i][0],component2=f['rank2']['loadings'][i][1]))
pd.DataFrame(est).to_csv(R/'rank1_estimates.csv',index=False);pd.DataFrame(loads).to_csv(R/'rank2_loadings.csv',index=False)
lines=['# CryptBB label-free checkpoint selection experiment','',
'Completed on frozen predictions from **historical Model1-A epochs 1–20** and **v3 Model1-B epochs 1–16**, on the same 251 real images. These are different synthetic-generation versions, not matched A/B seeds of one experiment. B epochs after 16 are deliberately excluded. No training, stopping, generator or adopted selection policy was changed.','',
'## Findings and recommendation','',
'The method can rank checkpoints usefully, but **the factors are not calibrated estimates of absolute real accuracy on these runs**. Exact masked rank 1 chooses B epoch 13 (62/251, 24.70%, zero observed regret), but estimates its accuracy as 64.29%. It chooses A epoch 14 (47/251, 18.73%), five correct images below A’s best epoch 17. A’s automatic mask criterion never passes; its k=5 result is an explicit fallback. Both exact-kernel fits trigger the rank-2 structural flag.','',
'For the next prospectively frozen benchmark, I recommend **whole-string leave-one-out mode agreement with fractional tie credit as the simple baseline**, and masked exact rank 1 as an additional diagnostic, not a replacement accuracy estimator. The simple baseline selects A20 (49/251) and B13 (62/251), with 1.20 and 0.00 percentage-point regret here. This is a provisional recommendation made after inspecting these two runs, not evidence that this rule generalizes. Do not choose a new k or weight from the minimum regret in the sweep. When the mask criterion fails or rank 2 flags structure, report model-assumption failure rather than a trustworthy absolute accuracy. Cross-run agreement did not consistently improve choices.','',
'Character/edit scores measure string similarity, not exact-string correctness. Their factors are not accuracy estimators under the proposed independent-error identity; their large MAEs against exact accuracy are retained as requested model-mismatch diagnostics. The optional collision term is not fitted: it adds another confounded degree of freedom without anchors.','',
'## Main comparisons','',
'Percentages below are measured exact-string accuracy. Regret is best observed accuracy minus selected accuracy; correlations are descriptive across epochs.','',
'| Run | Rule | Kernel | Selected epoch | Correct / 251 | Accuracy | Regret (pp) | Spearman | Kendall | Best in top 3 | Factor MAE (pp) |',
'|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|']
methods=['mode_self_anytie','mode_self_fractional','mode_loo_anytie','mode_loo_fractional','pairwise_all','rank1_auto','cross_mode_fractional','cross_pairwise']
for run in ['Model1-A','Model1-B']:
 for method in methods:
  rr=df[(df.run==run)&(df.method==method)&(df.kernel=='exact')]
  for _,r in rr.iterrows():
   mae='—' if pd.isna(r.mae) else f'{100*r.mae:.2f}'
   lines.append(f'| {run} | {method} | exact | {r.selected_epoch} | {r.selected_correct} | {100*r.true_selected_accuracy:.2f}% | {100*r.regret:.2f} | {r.spearman:.3f} | {r.kendall:.3f} | {r.top3_contains_best} | {mae} |')
lines+=['',f'Full results: [{len(df)} method/kernel/k rows](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/summary.csv), including both tie rules, both mode kernels, all leave-neighbourhood masks, all pairwise/rank-1 kernels and all k values. Mode is defined only for exact strings or positions; there is no fabricated “edit mode.” Pairwise all includes the diagonal; masked means exclude it and normalize by each epoch’s number of eligible neighbours.','',
'## Frozen protocol and simulation gate','',
'All rules/constants and source hashes were saved before real selection. Predictions were hash-checked against their original freezes. Selection artifacts were persisted before the evaluation module opened scoring labels. `PredictionTable` contains no labels; the loader rejects any extra fields in per-image prediction records. Selection modules never import evaluation. Tests enforce this dependency boundary. A real-label inspection cannot be undone: these are retrospective data already discussed, so this is not a pristine blind validation.','',
'- Fixed seed: 4817. Bootstrap: 10,000 paired image resamples, same sampled image indices for selected and best.','- k grid: 0–5. Rank 1 masks every pair with |t−u| ≤ k. Median eligible triplets initialize bounded Gauss–Seidel coordinate updates; no eligible triplets uses a documented square-root mean-agreement fallback. All real rank-1 fits converged.','- Choose the smallest k whose mean absolute residual at distance k+1 is at most the far-distance residual plus max(0.005, 25% of that far residual). Far means distance ≥ max(k+2, ceil(n/2)). If none passes, retain k=5 and mark failure. This is a heuristic, not a confidence test.','- Rank 2 uses four fixed-seed bounded nonnegative least-squares starts on the same mask. Flag when relative MSE reduction >35% AND absolute RMSE reduction >0.003. This is an in-sample structural warning; more parameters naturally improve fit. No held-out residual claim or uniquely identified truth/trap component is made. Components are ordered by loading energy only.','- Mode ties: original any-candidate match and fractional 1/number-of-modes credit. Leave-one-out removes self; leave-neighbourhood-out removes t±k including self. All real predictions were length5; general positional voting uses maximum observed prediction length and explicit absence votes. Char pair similarity falls back to normalized edit similarity when lengths differ. Empty/empty similarity is 1. No target strings or true lengths enter selection.','- Calibration bins: [0,.2], (.2,.4], (.4,.6], (.6,.8], (.8,1]. Epoch13 “near” threshold: absolute error ≤0.03, fixed before scoring. No thresholds were tuned on the 251 labels.','',
'### Required tests','',
'All seven pytest tests passed before the successful real-data run (the required three simulations, edge kernels, tie/exclusion handling, module boundary and syntax). At m=2000: independent diverse errors recovered known accuracy with MAE **0.00868**, selecting the true best epoch13. A deliberately coupled late cluster made unmasked rank1 choose epoch19; masking k=5 recovered the true best epoch6. The planted-trap case improved rank2 MSE by **96.32%**, and the flag fired.','',
'**Important extra simulation finding:** the automatic k heuristic selected k=0 in the localized-cluster case and therefore still selected the wrong epoch19. A known sufficiently wide mask succeeds, but the automatic criterion does not reliably discover it. Its average over all pairs at a distance dilutes a cluster confined to late epochs. The independent simulation had no rank2 flag; both temporal coupling and traps triggered it. Thresholds were not retuned after discovering these limitations. See [simulation diagnostics](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/postrun_verification.json).','',
'One plotting-only syntax error occurred after the first selection freeze and before labels were read. That attempt is preserved in `results/cryptbb_A20_B16`. The corrected run is `results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified`; its scores/choices are exactly identical to the first freeze.','',
'## Robustness across k','',
'| Run | k | Exact selected epoch | Char selected epoch | Edit selected epoch |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for run in ['Model1-A','Model1-B']:
 for k in range(6):
  choices=[int(df[(df.run==run)&(df.method=='rank1')&(df.kernel==ker)&(df.k.astype(str)==str(k))].iloc[0].selected_epoch) for ker in ['exact','char','edit']]
  lines.append(f'| {run} | {k} | {choices[0]} | {choices[1]} | {choices[2]} |')
lines+=['','A exact changes from20 to15 to14 as the mask widens; none selects17. B exact selects13 for every k≥1, whereas char/edit move from13 to12 at k≥3. A fails the auto criterion for all three kernels. B passes at k=4 for each. See per-k criterion JSON and residual-distance CSV for the actual residual levels.','',
'## Rank-2 structure and absolute calibration','',
'| Run | Kernel | Automatic k | Criterion passed? | Rank1 MSE | Rank2 MSE | MSE improvement | Flag? |','|---|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for run in ['Model1-A','Model1-B']:
 for kernel in ['exact','char','edit']:
  c=read(R/f'{run}_{kernel}_k_selection.json');r=next(x for x in diag if x['run']==run and x['kernel']==kernel and x['k']==c['chosen_k'])
  lines.append(f'| {run} | {kernel} | {c["chosen_k"]} | {c["criterion_passed"]} | {r["rank1_mse"]:.6f} | {r["rank2_mse"]:.6f} | {100*r["relative_mse_improvement"]:.2f}% | {r["trap_component_flag"]} |')
lines+=['',
'Both exact-kernel fits flag extra structure. Evaluation-only attractor search found **61 A images and 44 B images** where a modal wrong whole string attracts at least half of the epochs. [Attractors with IDs and wrong strings](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/attractors.json). These counts corroborate repeated wrong answers, but do not identify a particular latent component as “the trap.” Temporal dependence, image difficulty and generator biases can all induce low-rank structure.','',
'For B epoch13, exact rank1 estimates **0.64288 versus actual 0.24701** (error0.39587), failing the predefined ±0.03 check. Exact-factor MAE across epochs is **0.31329 for A and0.27897 for B**. Char/edit factors are still farther from exact accuracy. Removing local temporal pairs does not remove systematic wrong collisions or item-difficulty effects. Even with errors independent conditional on image difficulty, E[p_t(image)p_u(image)] need not equal E[p_t(image)]E[p_u(image)]. The proposed factorization is an assumption, not an identity for general OCR.','',
'## Paired uncertainty','']
gap=read(R/'A17_vs_A19.json')
lines += [f'A17 is52/251; A19 is47/251. A19 uniquely gets3 right; A17 uniquely gets8 right. Exact two-sided McNemar **p={gap["mcnemar_p"]:.4f}**. A19 minus A17 is **{100*gap["difference"]:.2f}pp**, with paired percentile-bootstrap95% interval **[{100*gap["bootstrap_ci_low"]:.2f}, {100*gap["bootstrap_ci_high"]:.2f}]pp**. The observed five-image gap is **not distinguishable from zero at the conventional5% level** with this comparison. This does not prove equivalence.','',
'Every summary row contains selected-only/best-only counts, McNemar p, and a paired-bootstrap interval. “Best” is the empirical oracle chosen on these same251 images. These intervals are conditional on those fixed checkpoints and are not adjusted for oracle selection, multiple methods or repeated test inspection. Correlation p-values are intentionally not used as evidence: epochs are dependent and Spearman/Kendall coefficients are descriptive.','',
'## Mode calibration','',
'For unique whole-string modes, vote shares above80% correspond to correctness **7/11=63.64% for A** and **9/15=60.00% for B**. High temporal agreement is not a calibrated confidence probability. The small bins are noisy. Character bins condition on observed predicted positions, not edit-distance character accuracy; extra ground-truth characters outside those positions are not represented. Tied modes are reported separately using expected correctness under uniform tie-breaking, never a label-chosen tie.','',
'[Binned calibration](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/mode_calibration.csv) and per-image/per-position JSON files retain all denominators.','',
'## What to test next','',
'Two runs on one repeatedly inspected251-image pool are far too few to trust any rule. Do not count20 checkpoints as20 independent trials. A and B here also differ in generator version, so cross-run scoring is a domain/version comparison as well as a dependence reduction attempt.','',
'As a practical next-stage design, collect **at least20–30 additional independently trained runs**, for example5 seeds across4–6 fixed generator/domain conditions, and include at least3 real CAPTCHA families. Treat that as a pilot target, not a power guarantee. Freeze one primary selector and its failure/abstention policy first; use separate development runs for any revised residual criterion, then evaluate on held-out runs and preferably a new real-image pool. Use pilot variance of paired per-run regret to size the final study for a prespecified meaningful difference. More seeds on this same251-image pool alone will not establish domain generalization. No new training is authorized by this report.','',
'## Files and reproducibility','',
'- [Summary CSV](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/summary.csv): every applicable method/kernel/k, accuracy, regret, Spearman, Kendall, top3, MAE and uncertainty.','- [Per-epoch rank1 factors](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/rank1_estimates.csv), [rank2 loadings](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/rank2_loadings.csv), [full factorizations](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/factorizations.json).','- [Residual by distance](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/residual_by_distance.csv), agreement `.npy` matrices and cross-run matrices.','- [Selection freeze](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/selection_freeze.json), [protocol](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/pre_real_protocol.json), [verification](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/postrun_verification.json).','-24 PNGs: agreement/residual heatmaps, factor-vs-accuracy plots, residual-distance plots and rank2 loadings for both runs and all3 kernels. Representative [B exact accuracy](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/Model1-B_exact_accuracy.png) and [A exact heatmaps](results/cryptbb_A20_B16_verified/Model1-A_exact_heatmaps.png).','',
'From this folder: `python -m ckpt_select.run --run Model1-A --kernel exact --k auto`. Default execution is prediction-only. Add `--evaluate` to allow labels only after the selection freeze. Use a fresh `--out` directory; existing results are never overwritten. `--run all --kernel all --k auto --evaluate` reproduces the complete study. `python -m pytest -q` runs tests (this machine uses isolated `test_site` dependencies; see README).','',
'## References and scope','',
'The related spectral-ensemble literature derives label-free ranking under conditional independence and studies correlated groups; it does not validate this multiclass-string factor model or these two runs: [Parisi et al., 2014](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3910607/). Exact McNemar here uses the two-sided binomial test on discordant pairs, implemented with [SciPy binomtest](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.stats.binomtest.html). The suggested run count above is a study-design judgment, not a number asserted by those sources.','']
(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
print('Report written; derived estimate/loading CSVs saved; summary rows',len(df))
